        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Water-based deck stains usually dry to the touch within a couple of hours, take light foot traffic within a day and cure in about a week. Oil-based stains take roughly twice as long at each stage. Rain-safe times and recoat windows vary by product, so the label always comes first.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Most drying problems trace back to three choices: staining damp wood, staining in the wrong weather and applying too much stain. Wait for dry boards and a clear forecast, work in the shade, apply thin coats and wipe back the excess, and the clock will mostly take care of itself.
          </p>
        </div>

